WEBVTT

00:01:29.169 --> 00:01:31.899
I hereby pass sentence
upon the defendant...

00:01:32.572 --> 00:01:37.944
...Professor Washu.
The defendant shall be imprisoned

00:01:37.944 --> 00:01:40.714
in an Alpha-L model
restriction capsule and exiled.

00:01:40.714 --> 00:01:42.849
What? Hold on a minute!

00:01:42.849 --> 00:01:45.986
What did I do to deserve
such a heavy sentence?

00:01:45.986 --> 00:01:49.756
All I did was invent dimension-oscillating
bullets, an ozone-destroying cannon,

00:01:49.756 --> 00:01:53.089
and a time/space converting tachyon ray!

00:01:53.927 --> 00:01:57.021
Isn't that more than enough?

00:02:10.277 --> 00:02:11.945
Wake up, Washu.

00:02:11.945 --> 00:02:14.539
Good morning, Washu.

00:02:16.783 --> 00:02:19.911
Ah, that's right. I didn't
sleep at all last night.

00:02:24.591 --> 00:02:26.793
Hmm, everything is working well.

00:02:26.793 --> 00:02:30.464
Meta-drive, propulsion system,
and exterior coating.

00:02:30.464 --> 00:02:33.166
The third phase is now complete.

00:02:33.166 --> 00:02:34.634
Washu, you are a genius.

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:37.034
Washu, you are the greatest in the universe.

00:02:38.405 --> 00:02:40.566
It was a piece of cake!

00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:44.404
It won't be long now.

00:02:51.818 --> 00:02:54.855
Hey, Miss! I got this rice from
the black market just for you.

00:02:54.855 --> 00:02:58.158
It's a special blend of Gold
Sasanishiki and High Koshihikari.

00:02:58.158 --> 00:02:59.559
It's the very best kind.

00:02:59.559 --> 00:03:01.194
R-Really? Is this for me?

00:03:01.194 --> 00:03:03.997
But... in return... you know what I want.

00:03:03.997 --> 00:03:08.093
Oh, no. I don't think it's a good idea.

00:03:09.703 --> 00:03:13.673
Hi! It's time for Kid's Playtime.

00:03:13.673 --> 00:03:15.976
How are you all doing?

00:03:15.976 --> 00:03:18.706
Fine!

00:03:19.646 --> 00:03:21.481
What do you think you are doing?

00:03:21.481 --> 00:03:22.582
What?

00:03:22.582 --> 00:03:27.487
It was just getting to the juicy part... uh,
getting to a climactic moment.

00:03:27.487 --> 00:03:29.489
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:03:29.489 --> 00:03:32.459
What do you want anyway, Mihoshi?

00:03:32.459 --> 00:03:35.462
Ah, I was going to invite myself to lunch.

00:03:35.462 --> 00:03:38.192
We finished our lunch a while ago.

00:03:39.499 --> 00:03:41.797
What? You already have?

00:03:42.936 --> 00:03:44.704
Tenchi, you know what?

00:03:44.704 --> 00:03:48.241
Washu did not show up for breakfast or lunch.

00:03:48.241 --> 00:03:50.343
I wonder if there is anything wrong with her.

00:03:50.343 --> 00:03:53.608
Hmm, I'll go check on her then.

00:03:55.148 --> 00:03:56.672
Washu?

00:03:59.853 --> 00:04:02.185
What? She isn't here.

00:04:05.692 --> 00:04:08.695
Oh, Tenchi. What is it?

00:04:08.695 --> 00:04:13.564
Since you didn't come out to eat,
we were wondering what was going on.

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:16.469
Do you wanna know?

00:04:16.469 --> 00:04:17.804
You do want to know, don't you?

00:04:17.804 --> 00:04:19.829
Come on. Let us show you.

00:04:22.008 --> 00:04:23.944
Okay, then, come over here.

00:04:23.944 --> 00:04:25.378
Ah, but...

00:04:25.378 --> 00:04:28.142
I could actually use some help, so...

00:04:38.091 --> 00:04:39.292
Here it is!

00:04:39.292 --> 00:04:41.428
What... is this?

00:04:41.428 --> 00:04:45.565
This is my latest invention, Mecha-Washu.

00:04:45.565 --> 00:04:50.270
Mecha-Washu? What did
you make such a thing for?

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:53.473
Since I've been sealed
off for a long 700 years,

00:04:53.473 --> 00:04:56.209
I'm way behind schedule with my inventions.

00:04:56.209 --> 00:04:58.378
I needed an assistant, you see.

00:04:58.378 --> 00:05:02.148
This Mecha-Washu
is just as capable as I am,

00:05:02.148 --> 00:05:05.218
which means now I can work twice as fast.

00:05:05.218 --> 00:05:07.821
And is this finished?

00:05:07.821 --> 00:05:10.890
The only thing left to do
is to input my mind data.

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:12.292
And then what happens?

00:05:12.292 --> 00:05:14.761
Then it'll be finished, of course.

00:05:14.761 --> 00:05:16.463
Huh?

00:05:16.463 --> 00:05:19.232
How did you get in here?

00:05:19.232 --> 00:05:22.969
I just... came from the entrance.

00:05:22.969 --> 00:05:27.372
Tenchi and I got here through pseudo-space.

00:05:29.442 --> 00:05:31.978
Washu, what is this?

00:05:31.978 --> 00:05:38.051
Using excess energy from pseudo-space
this device duplicates digitized mind data.

00:05:38.051 --> 00:05:41.154
Hmm, is that right?

00:05:41.154 --> 00:05:43.790
Do you understand now?

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:45.959
You don't get it, do you?

00:05:45.959 --> 00:05:48.154
Get out of my way.

00:05:50.397 --> 00:05:54.868
Tenchi, I'm transferring the data now.

00:05:54.868 --> 00:05:58.538
Could you turn on the switch on
the bottom right of that console?

00:05:58.538 --> 00:06:01.307
Huh? Uh, is this it?

00:06:01.307 --> 00:06:03.677
No! The one below that.

00:06:03.677 --> 00:06:05.838
This must be it.

00:06:07.547 --> 00:06:09.315
Hmm, can this be it then?

00:06:09.315 --> 00:06:11.084
Oh, that's not right, how about this one?

00:06:11.084 --> 00:06:14.247
Hey! Don't play around with that!

00:06:20.593 --> 00:06:24.427
Oh, no. What do I do now?

00:06:39.145 --> 00:06:41.548
Look what you've done to me!

00:06:41.548 --> 00:06:44.039
I'm sorry.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:50.156
Great! No damage at all!

00:06:50.156 --> 00:06:53.293
I've done it! This is finally finished.

00:06:53.293 --> 00:06:54.828
Washu, you have done it!

00:06:54.828 --> 00:06:56.963
Washu, you are great!

00:06:56.963 --> 00:06:59.591
Okay, now. Move, Mecha-Washu.

00:06:59.733 --> 00:07:01.223
All right!

00:07:04.104 --> 00:07:08.507
Oh, yes, that's my girl. My creation is great.

00:07:13.113 --> 00:07:13.913
What?

00:07:13.913 --> 00:07:16.381
Is there something wrong?

00:07:22.288 --> 00:07:25.592
I'm getting kind of hungry.

00:07:25.592 --> 00:07:30.086
- Ah, you, too?
- Ah, you, too?

00:07:38.438 --> 00:07:40.599
What... is this?

00:07:41.708 --> 00:07:43.977
A blond hair?

00:07:43.977 --> 00:07:46.412
Is it possible that the
genetic data from this hair

00:07:46.412 --> 00:07:50.246
- got imprinted into Mecha-Washu?
- What happened?

00:07:53.086 --> 00:07:55.822
How could your mind data
be transferred instead of mine

00:07:55.822 --> 00:07:59.526
because of just one piece of hair?

00:07:59.526 --> 00:08:02.095
What kind of mind-data
structure do you have?

00:08:02.095 --> 00:08:04.928
Well, I'm sorry.

00:08:05.732 --> 00:08:07.400
The robot is gone!

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:08.902
What?

00:08:08.902 --> 00:08:10.737
It has to be somewhere within this area.

00:08:10.737 --> 00:08:12.105
We've got to find it.

00:08:12.105 --> 00:08:13.436
Uh-huh.

00:08:19.479 --> 00:08:21.538
It's empty.

00:08:27.253 --> 00:08:29.289
This is really the best meat we ever had.

00:08:29.289 --> 00:08:31.758
Come on. You want this, too.

00:08:31.758 --> 00:08:37.297
Oh, no! Not so fast!

00:08:37.297 --> 00:08:42.302
We are interrupting this regular
broadcast for an emergency broadcast.

00:08:42.302 --> 00:08:46.306
This just in. Robbers broke
into the Banana Bank in Kurashiki.

00:08:46.306 --> 00:08:49.542
What happened to the soap opera?

00:08:49.542 --> 00:08:52.212
It was just getting down to the good part.

00:08:52.212 --> 00:08:55.340
Oh, my God. I have to do something about this.

00:09:05.325 --> 00:09:07.122
Upsy-daisy!

00:09:13.333 --> 00:09:16.234
Did I just come by here?

00:09:18.438 --> 00:09:21.669
How did it get out of that room?

00:09:23.176 --> 00:09:25.378
What was that?

00:09:25.378 --> 00:09:27.642
We are just seeing things.

00:09:33.052 --> 00:09:37.523
Oh, darn. I don't have
a car to get into the city.

00:09:37.523 --> 00:09:39.225
Hold it right there!

00:09:39.225 --> 00:09:40.426
What?

00:09:40.426 --> 00:09:41.794
Finally, I found you.

00:09:41.794 --> 00:09:45.031
Now let's go back to the lab, okay?

00:09:45.031 --> 00:09:50.367
Please don't stop me.
I have to go save the hostages.

00:09:52.038 --> 00:09:54.340
The bank is being robbed right now.

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:56.342
As a Galaxy Police Officer, I have to...

00:09:56.342 --> 00:09:58.878
Look at yourself! What part of you
is a Galaxy Police Officer anyway?

00:09:58.878 --> 00:10:02.515
Well, I think you'd better
leave it to the local police.

00:10:02.515 --> 00:10:04.918
We have to catch the suspects.

00:10:04.918 --> 00:10:07.086
- Shut up!
- Uh, all right.

00:10:07.086 --> 00:10:09.255
Oh, no, wait!

00:10:09.255 --> 00:10:14.093
If you try to keep me here any longer,
it will constitute an obstruction of justice.

00:10:14.093 --> 00:10:16.262
What are you talking about?

00:10:16.262 --> 00:10:21.100
All right. If it's necessary to
do this to get justice done...

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:22.602
Go on, Washu.

00:10:22.602 --> 00:10:24.370
Let's go, Washu.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:27.073
What? You traitors!

00:10:27.073 --> 00:10:29.075
Are you ready for this?

00:10:29.075 --> 00:10:32.879
A Mecha-Washu punch!

00:10:32.879 --> 00:10:35.848
Stop it! Stop it! Stop it!

00:10:37.417 --> 00:10:41.012
Huh? Come out.

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:55.791
I got her.

00:10:57.470 --> 00:10:59.439
Are you okay, Mihoshi?

00:10:59.439 --> 00:11:01.341
It hurts.

00:11:01.341 --> 00:11:04.344
What did you make such a weapon for?

00:11:04.344 --> 00:11:06.612
It's a defense mechanism, just in case.

00:11:06.612 --> 00:11:10.717
As a genius, I always have to
be prepared for the worst scenario.

00:11:10.717 --> 00:11:12.585
Uh-huh, she is a genius.

00:11:12.585 --> 00:11:15.019
Yup, a genius can't help it.

00:11:16.656 --> 00:11:19.682
Isn't she always creating the
worst possible scenario herself?

00:11:40.213 --> 00:11:42.782
You've got nowhere to hide now.

00:11:42.782 --> 00:11:47.446
Mecha-Washu beam!

00:11:48.154 --> 00:11:52.458
What's the commotion?
We can't hear the TV!

00:11:52.458 --> 00:11:54.093
Oh, sorry.

00:11:54.093 --> 00:11:56.323
Watch out!

00:12:02.368 --> 00:12:05.371
Isn't that just like a machine I invented?

00:12:05.371 --> 00:12:08.141
It has such great power.

00:12:08.141 --> 00:12:09.942
Washu, you are wonderful.

00:12:09.942 --> 00:12:13.312
Washu, you are great!

00:12:13.312 --> 00:12:15.280
Wipe that irritating smile off your face!

00:12:21.754 --> 00:12:26.191
Everybody seems to be having
fun as usual. Right, Ryo-Ohki?

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:32.498
Now I'm gonna have to...

00:12:32.498 --> 00:12:34.434
Use those special tactics, right, Washu?

00:12:34.434 --> 00:12:37.164
We are all behind you, Washu!

00:12:39.539 --> 00:12:41.666
We call this...

00:12:43.109 --> 00:12:45.907
...Operation Volleyball!

00:13:12.338 --> 00:13:14.407
Prepare to die!

00:13:14.407 --> 00:13:18.969
Nobody's ever survived
this atom-destroying ball!

00:13:19.545 --> 00:13:25.651
When someone spikes the ball
it disrupts the atoms of the target.

00:13:25.651 --> 00:13:29.822
It's a truly clever weapon.

00:13:29.822 --> 00:13:31.312
Okay!

00:13:31.824 --> 00:13:34.884
Here it comes!

00:13:35.495 --> 00:13:37.296
Oops!

00:13:37.296 --> 00:13:41.200
Oh, well! After 700 years without
practice my aim can't be perfect.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:43.794
Can't be perfect?

00:13:46.305 --> 00:13:48.474
Hey, what are you doing?

00:13:48.474 --> 00:13:49.308
It's coming.

00:13:49.308 --> 00:13:50.639
Huh?

00:13:51.677 --> 00:13:53.577
Here!

00:13:57.016 --> 00:13:59.152
What are you thinking, Ayeka?

00:13:59.152 --> 00:14:02.121
Oh, excuse me.

00:14:02.121 --> 00:14:04.555
Tenchi, it's coming at you.

00:14:07.226 --> 00:14:08.989
This is it!

00:14:10.796 --> 00:14:13.560
Attack!

00:14:15.468 --> 00:14:17.231
You missed me!

00:14:23.576 --> 00:14:25.737
My vegetable garden.

00:14:43.129 --> 00:14:45.398
Ah, I have no other choice.

00:14:45.398 --> 00:14:47.992
I really didn't wanna use this, though.

00:14:52.471 --> 00:14:53.539
What is it?

00:14:53.539 --> 00:14:55.775
It's the self-destruct device
for Mecha-Washu.

00:14:55.775 --> 00:14:57.710
You had that choice all along?

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:59.979
Why didn't you use that from the start?

00:14:59.979 --> 00:15:03.176
I didn't create Mecha-Washu
overnight, you know!

00:15:04.317 --> 00:15:06.419
Good-bye, Mecha-Washu.

00:15:06.419 --> 00:15:10.790
I wanted to conquer the universe with you.

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:13.258
Let's see...

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:24.831
Come to me, spare body.

00:15:37.717 --> 00:15:43.178
Oh, no! The spare body I was reserving.

00:15:55.201 --> 00:15:59.160
Ahh, I thought I was finished.

00:16:01.407 --> 00:16:03.175
Killing an officer is a very grave offense.

00:16:03.175 --> 00:16:06.838
You must be severely punished.

00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:12.583
Mecha-Washu beam!

00:16:20.393 --> 00:16:25.558
Ohh, what happened?

00:16:34.507 --> 00:16:38.344
It's way past our patrolling time.

00:16:38.344 --> 00:16:40.904
I wonder what Mihoshi is up to. Huh?

00:16:46.952 --> 00:16:52.224
You can't treat me like that!

00:16:52.224 --> 00:16:54.249
What is that?

00:16:56.662 --> 00:16:59.130
Ah, Kiyone!

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:03.602
Kiyone, listen to me!

00:17:03.602 --> 00:17:09.006
These guys are ganging up
on me and standing in my way.

00:17:10.042 --> 00:17:12.533
What the heck are you talking about?

00:17:13.846 --> 00:17:15.871
Kiyone, be careful!

00:17:29.161 --> 00:17:31.030
Washu, do something!

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:34.022
The spare body isn't
equipped with a self-destruct device.

00:17:37.837 --> 00:17:41.773
Does that robot have the mind of Mihoshi?

00:17:48.114 --> 00:17:50.810
Yeah, you guessed it.

00:17:53.819 --> 00:17:58.391
You are such a troublemaker!
Just one thing after another!

00:17:58.391 --> 00:18:00.859
I'm so sorry.

00:18:03.996 --> 00:18:09.024
- What are we going to do now?
- Kiyone, please help us.

00:18:10.436 --> 00:18:14.202
If the robot and Mihoshi truly think alike...

00:18:20.045 --> 00:18:21.847
Tenchi, this is gonna work, definitely.

00:18:21.847 --> 00:18:27.787
- What?
- Mihoshi, you'd better hurry.
It's almost starting now.

00:18:27.787 --> 00:18:29.948
Oh, no!

00:18:32.892 --> 00:18:34.860
Oh, I don't wanna miss anything.

00:18:35.694 --> 00:18:38.822
Oh, it's already time.

00:18:47.072 --> 00:18:49.336
What is it?

00:18:53.979 --> 00:18:57.383
Metamor-force!

00:18:57.383 --> 00:19:01.020
- Wow! Great!
- Yeah! Moldiver!

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:05.090
It's so cool! Go! Go, Moldiver!

00:19:05.090 --> 00:19:08.093
See, I told you it was gonna work.

00:19:08.093 --> 00:19:10.763
I see what you mean.

00:19:10.763 --> 00:19:14.133
Now where is the on/off switch?

00:19:14.133 --> 00:19:17.102
It's behind the neck.

00:19:17.102 --> 00:19:17.503
- Yay! Yay! Yay! Yay!

00:19:17.503 --> 00:19:21.273
- It's a great show, huh?
You are such a good girl.
- Yay! Yay! Yay! Yay!

00:19:21.273 --> 00:19:24.009
- Hold still for me, okay?
- Yay! Yay! Yay! Yay!

00:19:24.009 --> 00:19:27.279
- Here!
- Yay! Yay! Yay! Yay!

00:19:27.279 --> 00:19:34.947
Yay! Yay...

00:19:36.355 --> 00:19:41.660
Kiyone, you are an expert
at how Mihoshi's mind works.

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:46.065
It's not something I'm proud of.

00:19:46.065 --> 00:19:49.802
Everybody, dinner is ready!

00:19:49.802 --> 00:19:55.875
Oh, good. Dinnertime. I was starving.

00:19:55.875 --> 00:19:58.969
Ah, Washu, what's wrong with you?

00:19:59.578 --> 00:20:01.705
You're such an airhead.

00:20:08.988 --> 00:20:11.457
Washu, you are a genius.

00:20:11.457 --> 00:20:14.527
Washu, you are the
greatest in the world!

00:20:14.527 --> 00:20:16.562
I've finally done it.

00:20:16.562 --> 00:20:19.498
I made sure to only input
my mind data this time.

00:20:19.498 --> 00:20:23.901
I'll call this one Mecha-Washu II.

00:20:35.114 --> 00:20:37.207
Th-This must be...

00:20:38.484 --> 00:20:41.419
Ryo... Ryo-Ohki?

00:20:46.225 --> 00:20:48.750
This is funny!

00:22:55.654 --> 00:22:58.680
It's snowing. Come out
and see it quick, Ryo-Ohki!

00:22:59.858 --> 00:23:02.461
Brrr, it's freezing today.

00:23:02.461 --> 00:23:06.231
A day like this is perfect for having hot <i>sake.</i>

00:23:06.231 --> 00:23:09.034
Look, Ryoko is glued to the heater.

00:23:09.034 --> 00:23:13.238
One morning as snow falls silently the
long-forgotten memories come back to us.

00:23:13.238 --> 00:23:15.174
Next episode is: "No Need for Memories!"

00:23:15.174 --> 00:23:18.477
Yes, I remember. It was
snowing like this on that day...

00:23:18.477 --> 00:23:21.241
It's unquestionably melancholic.
